  "notes": "Cash-basis county. Receipts, disbursements, transfers and beginning/ending cash come from the Statement of Cash Receipts, Disbursements and Changes in Fund Balances - Governmental Funds (p4, Total Governmental Funds column; added by the v8 re-trim along with the Statement of Cash Basis Assets and Fund Balances p3 and the nonmajor combining statement p10). These tie to the Statement of Activities (p2) and the fund schedules (receipts 11,208,831; disbursements 12,286,657; beginning 13,835,411; ending 12,757,585 = cash 12,470,515 + restricted 287,070). Taxes 6,174,281 split by fund column (p4): Inheritance Tax 544,237, Visitors Promotion 36,637 (assumed lodging tax), rest (General 5,316,081 + Road & Bridge 28 + County Improvement 277,298) unlabeled; the earlier 28 shortfall was the Road & Bridge column. Interfund transfers in 3,070,000 (Road & Bridge) = out 2,500,000 (General) + 570,000 (Special Road), net zero. No business-type funds. Fund schedules for General, Road & Bridge, Inheritance Tax, Highway Buyback, Special Road, County Improvement and ARPA are in detail (actual and final budget, pp5-8). Nonmajor detail comes from the combining statement (p10), which gives the receipt type and function; budget_final for those lines is from the nonmajor budgetary comparison (p9, headed 'Year Ended June 30, 2024' but the figures are FY2025). Juvenile Diversion spending 8 is General Government per p10. Zero-activity lines omitted. Read pages 1-10 of 10. Road & Bridge disbursements (p6 budget schedule, 4,056,279; budget 6,669,223) are split in detail by the p4 Road & Bridge column: General Government 3,170,520, Principal and Interest 370,023, Capital Outlay 515,736."
